What is the most important OOP behavior shown by this code?

```java
interface Discount { int apply(int price); }
class NoDiscount implements Discount { public int apply(int price) { return price; } }
class TenOff implements Discount { public int apply(int price) { return price - 10; } }
Discount discount = new TenOff();
System.out.println(discount.apply(100));
```

Which option best explains the runtime behavior shown here?

